  <h2>What is GrapheneOS?</h2>
  <p>
    GrapheneOS is a non-profit, open-source mobile operating system based on the
    Android Open Source Project (<a href="/aosp">AOSP</a>) with substantial added
    hardening for privacy and security. It officially supports Google Pixel phones
    and keeps full compatibility with Android apps. Google's apps and services are
    not included by default, but they can be installed as fully sandboxed, regular
    apps without special system privileges.
  </p>

  <h2>GrapheneOS and rooting</h2>
  <p>
    GrapheneOS does not ship with root access, and its developers recommend against
    rooting: handing apps superuser access weakens the very security model the OS
    works to harden. Many people who consider rooting for privacy or bloatware
    removal find GrapheneOS covers those needs out of the box. Installing it does
    require unlocking the bootloader — and, unlike most custom-ROM installs, the
    bootloader can be locked again afterwards with full verified boot.
  </p>

  <h2>Start with a device scan</h2>
  <p>
    Whether GrapheneOS supports your phone comes down to the exact model. Our free
    <a href="/scan">browser-based scan</a> reads your device model and bootloader
    state over USB — the two checkpoints that decide whether a GrapheneOS install
    is even on the table.
  </p>
